CRITERION 1 — SaveWithRevisionIfScenario: comparison AND write inside ONE
held lock; no duplicated write path.  PASS.
  Command: Read internal/services/retirement/settings.go:748-764 and
           ApplyOverrides at :1187-1229.
  Evidence (settings.go:748-763, verbatim):
      func (sm *SettingsManager) SaveWithRevisionIfScenario(settings *models.WhatIfSettings, expectedScenario string) (int, error) {
          sm.mu.Lock()
          defer sm.mu.Unlock()
          if expectedScenario != "" && expectedScenario != sm.filename { ...return 0, &ScenarioConflictError{...} }
          if err := sm.saveInternalAndBump(settings); err != nil { sm.cache = nil; return 0, err }
          return sm.revision, nil
      }
  There is exactly one Lock and one deferred Unlock in the body; no
  sm.mu.Unlock() / RUnlock / second acquire appears between the comparison and
  saveInternalAndBump. Same shape as ApplyOverrides (:1192-1203: Lock, defer
  Unlock, then the identical expectedScenario != sm.filename guard).
  No second write path: `git diff HEAD -- internal/services/retirement/settings.go`
  is +32/-0 and contains no file-writing code — it calls saveInternalAndBump,
  the same locked helper SaveWithRevision (:727) and all 30-odd other mutation
  paths call. The write target is sm.filepath() (settings.go:828), derived from
  the same sm.filename the guard compares, under the same lock — so the guard
  names the state that decides the destination.

